[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2687990230","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2687990230","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2687990230,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gN3nW","user":{"login":"wareya","id":585488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/585488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya","html_url":"https://github.com/wareya","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T13:38:07Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T13:38:07Z","body":"For reference I'm using a dualsense (ps5 controller) that isn't particularly busted but isn't brand new either. So the amount of stick springiness I'm experiencing is somewhat surprising but not unusual, and not indicative of a dying/dead joystick.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2687990230/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688117622","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2688117622","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2688117622,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gOWt2","user":{"login":"wareya","id":585488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/585488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya","html_url":"https://github.com/wareya","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T14:25:31Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T14:29:46Z","body":"For more reference I used a joystick tester to test the threshold/deadzone value for left-stick menu navigation in various games I have installed:\n\nHonkai Star Rail: 55%\nGenshin Impact: 57%\nFinal Fantasy X HD Remaster: 82%\nFinal Fantasy 1 Pixel Remaster: 52~53%\nDragon Quest Builders 2: no analog stick menu navigation\nPhantom Brave PC: 82.5%ish\nFairy Fencer F: Refrain Chord: 58%\nKlonoa (launcher): 54%\nKlonoa Door To Phantomile (PC port): 50%\nAtelier Sophie DX: no analog stick menu navigation\nAtelier Ryza: 18%; also, navigating the settings menus is REALLY annoying. it's actively difficult to not accidentally trigger left/right and cause the value of a setting to change. On some menus I can get the backlash input glitch to happen.\nUtawarerumono: Mask of Deception: 38%\nFinal Fantasy XV Windows Edition: no analog stick menu navigation\nTales of Vesperia: Definitive Edition: 64%\n\nAlmost all of these are above 50%. Games that probably went through aggressive AAA-esque console release QA testing generally have thresholds in the 65% to 85% range. The only one close to 20% is Atelier Ryza, where it causes problems.\n\nTrivia: the dualsense has a feature where if I hold the PS button and move the analog stick up or down it changes the volume of my PC's default audio device. The tilt threshold where this happens is at 95%.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688117622/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688336969","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2688336969","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2688336969,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gPMRJ","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T15:38:48Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T15:38:48Z","body":"The proposal for that change had tests done on a bunch of AAA games with much lower deadzone values that the ones you measured: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7069#issuecomment-1623721743\n\nI noticed most of the games you tested seem to be Japanese or Chinese, while the ones in the linked comment are US/European. Would that be a cultural difference maybe in how people use the analog stick?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688336969/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688360387","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2688360387","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2688360387,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gPR_D","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T15:46:51Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T15:46:51Z","body":"Perhaps it's a difference between UI vs ingame deadzones?\nI'm not sure which https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7069#issuecomment-1623721743 tested, but it sounds like @wareya is mostly concerned about UI use.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688360387/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688388649","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2688388649","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2688388649,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gPY4p","user":{"login":"wareya","id":585488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/585488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya","html_url":"https://github.com/wareya","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T15:56:42Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T15:56:42Z","body":"Yes, it's a difference between UI and ingame deadzones specifically. This issue is not about the ingame deadzone behavior, only UI.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688388649/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688389866","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2688389866","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2688389866,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gPZLq","user":{"login":"wareya","id":585488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/585488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya","html_url":"https://github.com/wareya","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T15:57:08Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T15:57:08Z","body":"(The games I cited have relatively normal ingame deadzones in the 5%~30% range.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688389866/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688397266","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2688397266","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2688397266,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gPa_S","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T15:59:46Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T15:59:46Z","body":"The problem then is likely that Godot only has a single default deadzone value for both UI and in-game events. It seems like the default was change to be better for in-game events, but also affected UI ones. Maybe it could be changed back to `0.20` for `ui_*` events specifically.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688397266/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688397989","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2688397989","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2688397989,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gPbKl","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T16:00:01Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T16:00:01Z","body":"See my comment here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97281#issuecomment-2688391556","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688397989/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688424202","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2688424202","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2688424202,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gPhkK","user":{"login":"wareya","id":585488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/585488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya","html_url":"https://github.com/wareya","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T16:09:03Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T16:09:03Z","body":"I think it would be best to not have a project-level UI threshold setting; sometimes for different inputs you want different thresholds for UI actions, in particular triggers and sticks feel very different. It would make sense for me to play a game where the trigger threshold is at 35% and the stick threshold is at 80%, for example. (Yes, lots of games use triggers, not just bumpers, for menu navigation these days.)\n\nFor the CharacterBody3D script, it could be changed to use the optional argument of `Input.get_vector` that lets it specify the deadzone.\n\nFor the 2D one, `Input.get_axis` doesn't have a deadzone argument, but maybe it could use `get_vector` with an explicit deadzone and just use the x component?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688424202/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688500550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2688500550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2688500550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gP0NG","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T16:34:55Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T16:34:55Z","body":"Please see if #103364 is a good compromise to restore safe deadzones for `ui_*` actions (and axis `pressed` state which was also changed in #99135 but similarly I'm not sure it's a good idea - feedback welcome).\n\nTiming is pretty short if we want to address this regression for 4.4, so either we find a good compromise that's safe, or revert those two PRs to go back to the 4.3 behavior for now.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688500550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688558301","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103360#issuecomment-2688558301","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103360","id":2688558301,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gQCTd","user":{"login":"wareya","id":585488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/585488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya","html_url":"https://github.com/wareya","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wareya/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T16:56:27Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T16:58:47Z","body":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103364 is a fair compromise and the one that I would probably personally make. Testing my test project in it, it brings the analog stick backlash behavior back to how it acted in 4.3; I still get glitchy backlash inputs once in a while, but they're relatively uncommon rather than the default occurrence.\n\nCould maybe follow up with changes to the character controller example scripts? But I wouldn't expect that in the same PR, and it's not super important either way since they'll just work how they did in 4.3.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688558301/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]